[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m To solve for \(\tan\left(x + \frac{\pi}{4}\right)\) given that \(\tan x = 2\), we can use the tangent addition formula. The formula for the tangent of a sum of two angles is:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \tan\left(x + \frac{\pi}{4}\right) = \frac{\tan x + \tan \frac{\pi}{4}}{1 - \tan x \tan \frac{\pi}{4}}
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m We know that \(\tan \frac{\pi}{4} = 1\). Substituting \(\tan x = 2\) and \(\tan \frac{\pi}{4} = 1\) into the formula, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \tan\left(x + \frac{\pi}{4}\right) = \frac{2 + 1}{1 - 2 \cdot 1} = \frac{3}{1 - 2} = \frac{3}{-1} = -3
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Therefore, the value of \(\tan\left(x + \frac{\pi}{4}\right)\) is \(\boxed{-3}\).<|endoftext|>
