[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m A rectangular pool is $6\text{ m}$ wide, $12\text{ m}$ long and $4\text{ m}$ deep. If the pool is half full of water, what is the volume of water in the pool?
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m To determine the volume of water in the pool, we need to calculate the volume of a rectangular prism. The formula for the volume \( V \) of a rectangular prism is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ V = \text{length} \times \text{width} \times \text{height} \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Given the dimensions of the pool:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m - Width = 6 meters
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m - Length = 12 meters
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m - Depth = 4 meters
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m We can substitute these values into the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ V = 12 \, \text{m} \times 6 \, \text{m} \times 4 \, \text{m} \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m First, we multiply the length and the width:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ 12 \, \text{m} \times 6 \, \text{m} = 72 \, \text{m}^2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Next, we multiply the result by the depth:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ 72 \, \text{m}^2 \times 4 \, \text{m} = 288 \, \text{m}^3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Therefore, the volume of water in the pool is:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ \boxed{288} \] cubic meters.<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m [Ground Truth]
