[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m In scientific notation, \( 10^{100} \) can be written as \( 1.0 \times 10^{100} \), which means sixteen zeros (and possibly an extra zero if it's meant in a very high precision):
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
