[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m In my neighborhood, there are six streets. There are 10 houses on each side of each street. No house faces two different streets. How many houses are in my neighborhood?
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m To find the total number of houses in the neighborhood, we can break the problem down into several steps.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 1. **Determine the number of houses on one side of one street:**
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    - There are 10 houses on each side of each street.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    - Each street has 6 streets.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    - Therefore, the number of houses on one side of one street is:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m      10 \text{ houses/ street} \times 6 \text{ streets/ side} = 60 \text{ houses/ side}
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 2. **Determine the total number of houses on a single street in the neighborhood:**
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    - There are 6 streets in each neighborhood.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    - Therefore, the total number of houses on a single street in the neighborhood is:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m      60 \text{ houses/ side} \times 6 \text{ streets/ side} = 360 \text{ houses}
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 3. **Calculate the total number of houses in the neighborhood:**
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    - Since the neighborhood has six streets and the number of houses on each side of each street is the same, we can multiply the number of houses on one side by the number of streets in the neighborhood:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m      360 \text{ houses/ side} \times 6 \text{ streets/ side} = 2160 \text{ houses}
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Thus, the total number of houses in the neighborhood is \(\boxed{2160}\).<|endoftext|>
