[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m To find the least integer greater than $\sqrt{300}$, we start by simplifying the expression inside the square root:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \sqrt{300} = \sqrt{100 \times 3} = \sqrt{100} \times \sqrt{3} = 10\sqrt{3}
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Next, we need to determine the smallest integer that is greater than $10\sqrt{3}$. To do this, we can approximate $10\sqrt{3}$ to get a better sense of its value.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m First, calculate the approximate value of $\sqrt{3}$:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[
