[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Then, multiply this by 10:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 10\sqrt{3} \approx 10 \times 1.732 = 17.32
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Since we need the least integer greater than $10\sqrt{3}$, we round 17.32 up to the next integer, which is 18. Therefore, the least integer greater than $\sqrt{300}$ is:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \boxed{18}
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
