[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Paula invests $\$10,\!000$ for 5 years at an interest rate of $10\%$ per year. If the interest is simple interest, how much is her investment worth at the end of those five years?
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m To determine the value of Paula's investment at the end of 5 years, we need to use the formula for simple interest. The formula is:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ I = P \times r \times t \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m where:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m - \( I \) is the interest earned,
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m - \( P \) is the principal amount (the initial amount of money),
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m - \( r \) is the annual interest rate,
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m - \( t \) is the time the money is invested for in years.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m - The principal amount \( P = \$10,000 \),
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m - The annual interest rate \( r = 10\% = 0.10 \),
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m - The time \( t = 5 \) years.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m First, we calculate the interest earned:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ I = 10,000 \times 0.10 \times 5 \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ I = 10,000 \times 0.5 \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ I = 5,000 \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m The interest earned is \$5,000. Since the interest is simple, we subtract this from the principal to find the amount of money in the account at the end of 5 years:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ \text{Amount at the end of 5 years} = P - I \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ \text{Amount at the end of 5 years} = 10,000 - 5,000 \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ \text{Amount at the end of 5 years} = 5,000 \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Therefore, the amount of money Paula's investment is worth at the end of 5 years is \(\boxed{5000}\).<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \$15,\!000
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
