[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m To solve this problem, we first need to find the value of \(10N\), \(100N\), \(1000N\), and \(10,000N\) in terms of their respective floors.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ N = \frac{1}{3} \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m We have:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ 10N = 10 \times \frac{1}{3} = \frac{10}{3} \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ 100N = 100 \times \frac{1}{3} = \frac{100}{3} \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ 1000N = 1000 \times \frac{1}{3} = \frac{1000}{3} \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ 10,000N = 10000 \times \frac{1}{3} = \frac{10000}{3} \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Next, we need to find the floor values of these expressions:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ \lfloor 10 \times \frac{1}{3} \rfloor = \lfloor \frac{10}{3} \rfloor = \lfloor 3.3333\ldots \rfloor = 3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ \lfloor 100 \times \frac{1}{3} \rfloor = \lfloor \frac{100}{3} \rfloor = \lfloor 33.3333\ldots \rfloor = 33 \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ \lfloor 1000 \times \frac{1}{3} \rfloor = \lfloor \frac{1000}{3} \rfloor = \lfloor 333.3333\ldots \rfloor = 333 \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ \lfloor 10,000 \times \frac{1}{3} \rfloor = \lfloor \frac{10,000}{3} \rfloor = \lfloor 3333.3333\ldots \rfloor = 3333 \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Now, we sum these floor values:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ 3 + 33 + 333 + 3333 = 3 + 33 + 333 + 3333 = 3700 \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Thus, the value of \(\lfloor 10N \rfloor + \lfloor 100N \rfloor + \lfloor 1000N \rfloor + \lfloor 10,000N \rfloor\) is \(\boxed{3700}\).<|endoftext|>
