[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m To find the greatest prime factor of 221, we can follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 1. **Prime Factorization**:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    - First, we need to find the prime factors of 221.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    - We start by checking if 221 is divisible by the smallest prime number, which is 2.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m      - 221 is odd, so it is not divisible by 2.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    - Next, we check divisibility by 3. The sum of the digits of 221 is \(2 + 2 + 1 = 5\), which is not divisible by 3.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m      - 221 does not end in 0 or 5, so it is not divisible by 3.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    - Check divisibility by 5. Since 221 does not end in 0 or 5, it is not divisible by 5.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    - Next, we check divisibility by 7.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m      - \(221 \div 7 \approx 31.5714\), which is not an integer.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    - Check divisibility by 11. The alternating sum of the digits of 221 is \(2 - 2 + 1 = 1\), which is not divisible by 11.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m      - \(221 \div 11 \approx 20.0909\), which is not an integer.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    - Check divisibility by 13.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m      - \(221 \div 13 \approx 17.6154\), which is not an integer.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    - Check divisibility by 17.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m      - \(221 \div 17 = 12.3529\), which is not an integer.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    - Check divisibility by 19.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m      - \(221 \div 19 = 11.1578\), which is not an integer.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    - Check divisibility by 23.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m      - \(221 \div 23 = 9.4786\), which is not an integer.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    Since 221 is not divisible by any of these prime numbers, 221 itself cannot be expressed as a product of any prime numbers.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 2. **Prime Factors of Greater Numbers**:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    - We need to consider prime factors less than the square root of 221 (approximately 14.847) to ensure we find the greatest prime factor.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    - We check from the smallest primes down to 13, 11, 7, and 5:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m      - \(221 \div 5 \approx 44.2\) (not an integer),
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m      - \(221 \div 7 \approx 31.5\) (not an integer),
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m      - \(221 \div 11 \approx 20.09\) (not an integer),
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m      - \(221 \div 13 \approx 17.61\) (not an integer),
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m      - \(221 \div 17 \approx 11.15\) (not an integer),
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m      - \(221 \div 19 \approx 11.53\) (not an integer).
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    We continue this process and find that 11 is the greatest prime factor of 221.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Therefore, the greatest prime factor of 221 is \(\boxed{11}\).<|endoftext|>
