[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m To find the matrix \(\mathbf{M}\) that satisfies the system of equations \(\mathbf{M} \mathbf{i} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 3 \\ -8 \end{pmatrix}\), \(\mathbf{M} \mathbf{j} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 5 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}\), and \(\mathbf{M} \mathbf{k} = \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ -1 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}\), we need to determine the values of the columns of \(\mathbf{M}\). Let's denote \(\mathbf{M} = \begin{pmatrix} a & b & c \\ d & e & f \\ g & h & i \end{pmatrix}\).
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m First, we use the equation \(\mathbf{M} \mathbf{i} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 3 \\ -8 \end{pmatrix}\). This gives us the following system of equations:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ a \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 0 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} + b \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 5 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix} + c \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 0 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 3 \\ -8 \end{pmatrix}. \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m This can be written as:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ \begin{pmatrix} a \\ b \\ c \end{pmatrix} + \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 5 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix} + \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 0 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 3 \\ -8 \end{pmatrix}. \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m So, we get the equations:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ a + 0 + 0 = 2 \implies a = 2, \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ b + 5 + 0 = 3 \implies b + 5 = 3 \implies b = -2, \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ c - 2 + 4 = -8 \implies c - 2 = -8 \implies c = -6. \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Thus, the first column of \(\mathbf{M}\) is \(\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -2 \\ -6 \end{pmatrix}\).
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Next, we use the equation \(\mathbf{M} \mathbf{j} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 5 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}\). This gives us the following system of equations:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ d \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 0 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} + e \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 5 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix} + f \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 0 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 5 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}. \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m This can be written as:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ \begin{pmatrix} d \\ e \\ f \end{pmatrix} + \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 5 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 5 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}. \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m So, we get the equations:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ d = 0, \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ e + 5 = 5 \implies e = 0, \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ f - 2 = -2 \implies f = 0. \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Thus, the second column of \(\mathbf{M}\) is \(\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 0 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}\).
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Finally, we use the equation \(\mathbf{M} \mathbf{k} = \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ -1 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}\). This gives us the following system of equations:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ g \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 0 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} + h \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 5 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix} + i \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 0 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ -1 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}. \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m This can be written as:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ \begin{pmatrix} g \\ h \\ i \end{pmatrix} + \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 5 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ -1 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}. \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m So, we get the equations:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ g = 7, \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ h - 1 = -1 \implies h = 0, \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ i + 4 = 4 \implies i = 0. \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Thus, the third column of \(\mathbf{M}\) is \(\begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ 0 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}\).
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Therefore, the matrix \(\mathbf{M}\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ \mathbf{M} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & -2 & -6 \\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\ 7 & 0 & 0 \end{pmatrix}. \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m The final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[
