[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m The function $f$ is defined on positive integers as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[f(n) = \left\{
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \begin{array}{cl}
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m n + 10 & \text{if $n < 10$}, \\
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m f(n - 5) & \text{if $n \ge 10$}.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \right.\]Find the maximum value of the function.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m To find the maximum value of the function \( f(n) \), we need to analyze the function based on the given rule:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[ 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m f(n) = \left\{
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \begin{array}{cl}
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m n + 10 & \text{if } n < 10, \\
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m f(n - 5) & \text{if } n \ge 10.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \right.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Given this rule, we can start by checking the value of \( f(n) \) for \( n \) less than 10. According to the first case, since \( n < 10 \), we apply \( f(n) = n + 10 \).
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m So, \( f(1) = 1 + 10 = 11 \).
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Next, since \( n \ge 10 \), we apply the second case and get \( f(n-5) \). The only integer in the range \( 10 \le n-5 \le 9 \) is \( n-5 = 5 \), so \( f(5) = 5 + 10 = 15 \).
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Now, let's check \( n \ge 6 \) for completeness:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m For \( n = 6 \), it's clear that \( n \ge 10 \), so \( f(6) = f(6-5) = f(1) = 11 \).
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m For \( n = 7 \), \( n \ge 10 \), so \( f(7) = f(7-5) = f(2) \). But since \( 2 < 10 \), \( f(2) = 2 + 10 = 12 \).
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m For \( n = 8 \), \( n \ge 10 \), so \( f(8) = f(8-5) = f(3) \), and since \( 3 < 10 \), \( f(3) = 3 + 10 = 13 \).
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m For \( n = 9 \), \( n \ge 10 \), so \( f(9) = f(9-5) = f(4) \). Since \( 4 < 10 \), \( f(4) = 4 + 10 = 14 \).
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m For \( n = 10 \), \( n < 10 \), so \( f(10) = 10 + 10 = 20 \).
