[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 2. Number tiles containing a digit.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 3. Sorted stacks with chips of the digits $d_1, \cdots, d_k$. No false edges in the 2-D plane. $d_i$ values are distinct.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 4. Bit coins with a low-loss probability of an output.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 5. Slow or fast laser gun
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 6. The robot can only output the full third component / digits/digits position. Therefore, in order to distinguish a number tile from a digit tag, a sufficiently accurate precision in the output is required. You may assume that the layout of the tile (number) respects the scratches.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 7. If the tile number is divisible by 5, count as 1, otherwise count as 0.
