[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m To find the remainder when \(P(x) = x^4 - 7x^3 + 9x^2 + 16x - 13\) is divided by \(Q(x) = (x-3)\), we can use the Remainder Theorem. The Remainder Theorem states that the remainder of the division of a polynomial \(P(x)\) by \(x - c\) is \(P(c)\). In this case, since we are dividing by \(x-3\), we can directly use \(P(3)\).
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Let's proceed step-by-step:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 1. Substitute \(x = 3\) into the polynomial \(P(x)\):
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    P(3) = 3^4 - 7 \cdot 3^3 + 9 \cdot 3^2 + 16 \cdot 3 - 13
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 2. Calculate each term:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    3^4 = 81
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    3^3 = 27
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    3^2 = 9
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    16 \cdot 3 = 48
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    So,
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    P(3) = 81 - 7 \cdot 27 + 9 \cdot 9 + 48 - 13
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 3. Perform the multiplications:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    7 \cdot 27 = 189
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    9 \cdot 9 = 81
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    48 \cdot 3 = 144
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    Therefore,
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    P(3) = 81 - 189 + 81 + 144 - 13
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 4. Combine the terms:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    81 - 189 + 81 + 144 - 13 = (81 + 144) - (189 + 81) - 13
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    = 225 - 270 - 13
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    = -48 - 13
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    = -61
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m So, the remainder when \(x^4 - 7x^3 + 9x^2 + 16x - 13\) is divided by \(x-3\) is \(\boxed{-61}\).<|endoftext|>
