[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Compute $i^{600} + i^{599} + \cdots + i + 1$, where $i^2=-1$.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m To compute \( i^{600} + i^{599} + \cdots + i + 1 \), we start by recognizing that the powers of \( i \) repeat every 4 terms in the set \(\{1, i, -1, -i\}\). Therefore, we can simplify each term in the sum to \(-1\), \(i\), \(-1\), and \(i\), respectively.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m The sum \( i^{600} + i^{599} + \cdots + i + 1 \) then becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m -1 + i - 1 + i + \cdots + 1 + 1
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Since there are 600 terms in total, each of \(-1\) and \(1\) appears exactly half of the time. Therefore, there are 600 terms of \(-1\) and 600 terms of \(1\).
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m The sum of 600 terms of \(-1\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m -1 \times 600 = -600
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m The sum of 600 terms of \(1\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 1 \times 600 = 600
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \]
