[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m We need to find $JL$ given that $\angle JKL = 90^\circ$, $KL = 8$, and $\tan K = \frac{15}{8}$.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m To solve this, we'll use the definition of the tangent function in a right triangle. The tangent of an angle in a right triangle is the ratio of the length of the opposite side to the length of the adjacent side. Therefore, we can write:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \tan K = \frac{\text{opposite}}{\text{adjacent}} = \frac{KL}{JL}
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m - $KL = 8$
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m - $\tan K = \frac{15}{8}$
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m We substitute these values into the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \frac{15}{8} = \frac{8}{JL}
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m To solve for $JL$, we can cross-multiply and cross-multiply:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 15 \times JL = 8 \times 8
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 15JL = 64
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m To isolate $JL$, we divide both sides by 15:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m JL = \frac{64}{15}
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m So, the length of $JL$ is:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \boxed{\frac{64}{15}}
