[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m To simplify the expression \(\cos \frac{2 \pi}{13} + \cos \frac{6 \pi}{13} + \cos \frac{8 \pi}{13}\), we start by using the sum-to-product identities for cosines. The sum-to-product identities are:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \cos A + \cos B = 2 \cos \left( \frac{A+B}{2} \right) \cos \left( \frac{A-B}{2} \right)
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m First, we pair the terms \(\cos \frac{2 \pi}{13}\) and \(\cos \frac{8 \pi}{13}\):
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \cos \frac{2 \pi}{13} + \cos \frac{8 \pi}{13} = 2 \cos \left( \frac{\frac{2 \pi}{13} + \frac{8 \pi}{13}}{2} \right) \cos \left( \frac{\frac{2 \pi}{13} - \frac{8 \pi}{13}}{2} \right)
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Simplify the arguments of the cosine functions:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \cos \frac{2 \pi}{13} + \cos \frac{8 \pi}{13} = 2 \cos \left( \frac{10 \pi}{26} \right) \cos \left( \frac{-6 \pi}{26} \right) = 2 \cos \left( \frac{5 \pi}{13} \right) \cos \left( \frac{3 \pi}{13} \right)
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Next, we pair \(\cos \frac{6 \pi}{13}\) and \(\cos \frac{10 \pi}{13}\):
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \cos \frac{2 \pi}{13} + \cos \frac{10 \pi}{13} = 2 \cos \left( \frac{\frac{2 \pi}{13} + \frac{10 \pi}{13}}{2} \right) \cos \left( \frac{\frac{2 \pi}{13} - \frac{10 \pi}{13}}{2} \right)
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Simplify the arguments of the cosine functions:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \cos \frac{2 \pi}{13} + \cos \frac{10 \pi}{13} = 2 \cos \left( \frac{\frac{12 \pi}{13}}{2} \right) \cos \left( \frac{-6 \pi}{13} \right) = 2 \cos \left( \frac{6 \pi}{13} \right) \cos \left( \frac{6 \pi}{13} \right) = 2 \cos^2 \left( \frac{6 \pi}{13} \right)
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Now, we combine all the simplified terms:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \cos \frac{2 \pi}{13} + \cos \frac{6 \pi}{13} + \cos \frac{8 \pi}{13} = 2 \cos \left( \frac{5 \pi}{13} \right) \cos \left( \frac{3 \pi}{13} \right) + 2 \cos^2 \left( \frac{6 \pi}{13} \right)
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Factor out the common term \(2\) from the last two terms:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \cos \frac{2 \pi}{13} + \cos \frac{6 \pi}{13} + \cos \frac{8 \pi}{13} = 2 (\cos \left( \frac{5 \pi}{13} \right) \cos \left( \frac{3 \pi}{13} \right) + \cos^2 \left( \frac{6 \pi}{13} \right))
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m To simplify further, we use the identity \(\cos^2 x = \frac{1 + \cos 2x}{2}\):
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \cos^2 \left( \frac{6 \pi}{13} \right) = \frac{1 + \cos \left( \frac{12 \pi}{13} \right)}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Thus, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \cos \frac{2 \pi}{13} + \cos \frac{6 \pi}{13} + \cos \frac{8 \pi}{13} = 2 \left( \cos \left( \frac{5 \pi}{13} \right) \cos \left( \frac{3 \pi}{13} \right) + \frac{1 + \cos \left( \frac{12 \pi}{13} \right)}{2} \right)
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Simplify the argument of the second cosine:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \cos \left( \frac{5 \pi}{13} \right) \cos \left( \frac{3 \pi}{13} \right) = \frac{1}{2} \sin \left( \frac{12 \pi}{13} \right)
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m The term \(\cos \frac{12 \pi}{13}\) is a multiple of \(\pi\) and can be simplified using the identity \(\cos \left( \pi - x \right) = -\cos x\):
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \cos \frac{12 \pi}{13} = \cos \left( \pi - \frac{1 \pi}{13} \right) = -\cos \frac{\pi}{13}
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Thus, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \cos \left( \frac{5 \pi}{13} \right) \cos \left( \frac{3 \pi}{13} \right) = \frac{1}{2} \sin \left( \frac{12 \pi}{13} \right) = \frac{1}{2} \sin \left( \pi - \frac{\pi}{13} \right) = \frac{1}{2} \cos \frac{\pi}{13}
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Substitute back:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 2 \left( \frac{1}{2} \cos \frac{\pi}{13} + \cos \frac{\pi}{13} \right) = 2 \cdot \cos \frac{\pi}{13} \left( 1 + \frac{1}{2} \right) = 2 \cdot \cos \frac{\pi}{13} \cdot \frac{3}{2} = 3 \cos \frac{\pi}{13}
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Therefore, the simplified expression is:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \boxed{3 \cos \frac{\pi}{13}}
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
