[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Find the sum of the rational roots of $g(x)=x^3-9x^2+16x-4$.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m To find the sum of the rational roots of the polynomial \( g(x) = x^3 - 9x^2 + 16x - 4 \), we first need to identify all the rational roots of the polynomial. A rational root, if it exists, must be of the form \( \frac{p}{q} \), where \( p \) is a factor of the constant term (-4) and \( q \) is a factor of the leading coefficient (1).
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m The factors of -4 are: \( \pm 1, \pm 2, \pm 4 \).
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m The factors of 1 are: \( \pm 1 \).
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m We will test each factor \( p \) to see if \( q = 1 \) is a root of the polynomial. If \( q \) is 1, we can then determine the corresponding \( p \).
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Let's test:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 1. \( p = 1 \):
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    1 \cdot 4 = 4 \neq -4 \quad \text{(not a root, try another factor)}
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 2. \( p = -1 \):
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    -1 \cdot 4 = -4 \quad \text{(a root! continue)}
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 3. \( p = 2 \):
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    2 \cdot 2 = 4 \neq -4 \quad \text{(not a root, try another factor)}
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 4. \( p = -2 \):
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    -2 \cdot 2 = -4 \quad \text{(a root! continue)}
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 5. \( p = 4 \):
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    4 \cdot 1 = 4 \neq -4 \quad \text{(not a root, try another factor)}
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 6. \( p = -4 \):
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    -4 \cdot 1 = -4 \quad \text{(a root! continue)}
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m We have found two rational roots \( 4 \) and \( -4 \). To find the sum of the rational roots, we add these values together:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 4 + (-4) = 0
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Therefore, the sum of the rational roots of \( g(x) = x^3 - 9x^2 + 16x - 4 \) is \(\boxed{0}\).<|endoftext|>
