[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m The probability that Asha will lose a game is $\frac{4}{9}$. If it is impossible to tie, what is the probability that Asha will win the game? Express your answer as a common fraction.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m To determine the probability that Asha will win the game, we need to consider the given information and the possible outcomes. According to the problem, the probability that Asha will lose a game is \(\frac{4}{9}\). Since it is impossible to tie, Asha wins a game if and only if Asha loses.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m The probability that Asha will lose a game can be calculated by subtracting the probability that asha will win a game from 1. This is because if Asha wins, she will not lose.
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m P(\text{Asha loses}) = 1 - P(\text{Asha wins}) = 1 - \frac{4}{9}
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Simplify the expression:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 1 - \frac{4}{9} = \frac{9}{9} - \frac{4}{9} = \frac{5}{9}
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m Thus, the probability that Asha will win the game is \(\boxed{\frac{5}{9}}\).<|endoftext|>
