[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 52, 51, 49, \cdots, 46 + \frac{49}{40}
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m To find the sum of the first 49 terms of an arithmetic sequence with first term a = 52 and common difference d = -1, and with the formula \( S_n = \frac{n}{2}(2a + (n-1)d) \), we can use the formula for an arithmetic series and algebraic manipulation:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m S_n = \frac{40}{2}(100) = 20 \cdot 100 = 2000
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
