[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m To find the age of the oldest Wilson child, we need to use the information given about the average age of the three Wilson children. Here's the step-by-step process:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 1. **Understand the average age formula:**
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    The average age of the three Wilson children is 7 years. This means the sum of their ages divided by 3 is 7. We can write this as:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \frac{\text{age of child 1} + \text{age of child 2} + \text{age of child 3}}{3} = 7
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m 2. **Substitute the known ages:**
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    We know the ages of the first two children:
[36m(main_task pid=3102311)[0m    \[
